# G091 — PDF Generator

*v2. See `pdf-generator.md` for prose: pagination as flow layout
kernel, word-wrap as the paragraph's own layout, rendered document
as renderer-independent IR, heading-orphan avoidance built in.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Report

[vault-report @preferred-format
    IN ORDER TO
        gather report-tagged sections from the vault graph
        paginate them into a renderer-agnostic Page IR
        and hand off to whichever emitter the vault has configured

    @doc <- [pdf[new {width: 80, height: 66}]]
    [pdf[heading   {doc: @doc, text: "Weekly Report", level: 1}]]
    [pdf[paragraph {doc: @doc, text: @weekly-summary}]]

    @sections <- [vault[find {tag: "report"}]]
    for @section in @sections
        [pdf[heading   {doc: @doc,
                         text: @section:title, level: 2}]]
        [pdf[paragraph {doc: @doc, text: @section:body}]]

    @pages <- [pdf[render {doc: @doc}]]

    [renderer[emit {format: @preferred-format, pages: @pages}]]
]

---

## Verb Surface

[pdf
    new             {width, height}
    heading         {doc, text, level}                  ;; fluent
    paragraph       {doc, text}
    spacer          {doc, height}
    page-break      {doc}
    render          {doc}                               ;; -> [Page]
    page-count      {doc}
    wrap-text       {text, width}                       ;; -> [String]
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: pagination as `where`-fits flow

[pdf[render {doc: @doc}]
    IN ORDER TO
        place each block on the current page where it fits
        or roll to a new page where it does not
        honouring orphan-prevention for headings

    blocks of @doc
        placed at y on current page
        where block-height fits in remaining height
            -> place and advance y
        where block is a heading and remaining height is less than
             (heading lines + 1 trailing blank)
            -> start new page, then place heading
        otherwise
            -> start new page, then place block
]

This is the kernel every real PDF library (iText, ReportLab, LaTeX)
shares. G091 exposes only the kernel — fonts, glyphs, colour spaces,
binary encoding all layer above.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: wrap at word boundaries `where` possible

[pdf[wrap-text {text: @t, width: @w}]
    words of @t
        appended to current line
            where (current-line-length + 1 + word-length) ≤ @w
        otherwise
            -> emit current line, start new line with word
        where word-length is greater than @w alone
            -> emit word as its own (over-wide) line
               (truncation silently loses information; overflow is visible)
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    @doc <- [pdf[new {width: 40, height: 10}]]
    [pdf[heading   {doc: @doc, text: "Rosetta Stone", level: 1}]]
    [pdf[paragraph {doc: @doc,
                     text: "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. " +
                            "Pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs."}]]
    [pdf[heading   {doc: @doc, text: "Section 1", level: 2}]]
    [pdf[page-break {doc: @doc}]]
    [pdf[paragraph {doc: @doc,
                     text: "Content starts on a fresh page."}]]

    -> [pdf[render {doc: @doc}]]
    ;; -> two pages, layout deterministic across languages
]
